  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 25

Iteration 24 asked for amu execution of the prefix-argument count-loop
with `back-edge?` false, or keep the guard. This file takes the first
arm for that one function, and keeps the guard.

Do not overwrite 04-24.

## What ran

amu's `call-and-back-edge-module` now puts `:gmir/argument` and
`:gmir/constant acc0` before the preheader label, same as kotoba-mir
iteration 24. Phi predecessors stay `:test.label/preheader`. The jump
still sits in the preheader block.

`a-call-and-a-back-edge-in-one-function-execute`:

- production (no override): `[:all-vregs 8]` on both targets; kexe
  n∈{0,1,5,50} equals n, no `KEXE_TRAP`
- `with-redefs mir/back-edge?` → false: policy `:call-live` on both
  targets; the same kexe oracle, compile inside the override;
  `(pos? @calls)` so green is not an unapplied redef

Judah: `isa-execution-test` **18 tests, 688 assertions, 0 failures**.
Available ISAs: `[aarch64 x86_64]`. Slot count is not the claim.

## What this is not

Not predicate removal. One function executing on the scanner path is
encodings plus kexe for that fixture, not a license to drop
`back-edge?` for the suite. Production still all-vreg via the guard.

Not cfg-liveness. Not a spill-across-back-edge measurement. Allocator
code is unchanged (`ac14016d` / `69e364e`). deps.edn was not bumped.

## Pins

- amu `aa77f569c282e15e48d0d9c5825dcf19fddbf17b` (merge of
  `agent/scanner-exec-count-loop`, feature
  `a1baf555bb50a536d190cb243d017efe7afea561`).
  west-pin `64e3380b6e82993f0943a750308287895083b7ed`
- kotoba-mir not moved (`6ccc30eb4a90548c94bc62a912e91386197a069e`,
